    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 50 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, no failures or errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked household handling on `POST /api/owners` accordingly.\n\n**Core change \u2014 deterministic householdId** (`AssignHouseholdId.java`)\n- Now runs for *every* owner (no longer gated on `sharesHousehold`) and computes `householdId` as the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Owners with the same last name and postcode get the same id automatically, so the old back-fill/repository loop is gone.\n\n**New household-duplicate block** (`CheckHouseholdUnique.java` + exception/handler/escalation YAML, wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `assignHousehold` and `checkIdentity`)\n- Rejects with **409** when the computed `householdId` already belongs to an existing owner \u2014 *unless* the request declares `sharesHousehold`, which now merely bypasses this block (it no longer creates the link). The separate full `identityKey` check still applies to declared members, so a member repeating another's whole identity is still a 409 (Cp28).\n\n**Soft-match** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`)\n- A same-household existing owner (same computed `householdId`) is now skipped: a declared household member is not flagged as a suspected duplicate (`possibleDuplicate: false`).\n\n**Household-size input** (`AssignHouseholdMemberCount.java`)\n- Already keyed off `householdId`; it now groups by the always-computed id (doc updated). This is the household-size input feeding the membership level.\n\nThe household tests confirm the new contract: same lastName+postcode share the id (Cp11/Cp36), a second such owner is a 409 duplicate (Cp10/Cp35) unless it declares `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created and not flagged (Cp35), while full-identity duplicates still 409 regardless (Cp03/Cp25/Cp28).",
